title Kumara crypto re-grounded off Lindy onto structure; host, Puddle, Brix seated
prompt Keaton pushed back that Lindy is the wrong metaphor for security (past does not guarantee future when compute has never been more powerful); asked me to be confident in the decision; cleared me to key and bootstrap fake Puddle Kumara identities; offered a sudo nixos-rebuild if needed; asked to put Brix configuration in season planning with Brix code and docs molting; asked to update the host to Vultr SEA NixOS and make Claude Code the core software instead of Zed
think Agreed the Lindy metaphor was wrong for crypto and re-justified the SLH-DSA choice on a forward-looking threat model instead: the attacks that are actually rising (Oct 2025 lattice sieving, CRYPTO 2026 sign-based key recovery, AI-assisted cryptanalysis) exploit algebraic structure, and hashes are engineered to have none — so SLH-DSA has minimal exploitable structure, only a Grover quadratic dent from quantum (256-bit output covers it), and adds no new assumption since Grain already relies on the hash everywhere (seals, receipts, Merkle catalogs).
think Confirmed there is no mature independent signature family to hybridize with — code-based and multivariate broken, isogeny young, lattice eroding, symmetric/MPC not independent from the hash — so a second leg would be shakier than the floor; deferring it (agility kept) adds no risk. Stated confidence plainly and pinned the parameter set SLH-DSA-SHAKE-256s (NIST category 5).
think This is not a Lindy appeal — it is the smallest, best-understood attack surface with no added assumption, immune to the structural attacks that are climbing. The decision stands with a stronger justification.
obs Recorded Keaton's clearance to key and bootstrap fake/test Kumara identities in the constel/Puddle sandbox (consonant-only, non-@p-valid per placeholder-ship-names and FORA); the maintainer's real Kumara key stays the custody gate. This unblocks building and witnessing the crypto with real keypairs in the sandbox.
obs Seated Brix configuration into season planning (Brix code + Brix docs molt, riding the docs-compression round) in the decision-wave doc.
obs Updated GLOW_PROFILE.bron (gitignored, local source of truth): editor Claude Code, model claude-opus-4-8, voice Kyri, host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS, hand Daylight DC-1 (was Android Termux); new logs record editor Claude Code. Past dated logs keep their recorded editor/host, never rewritten.
obs No nixos-rebuild needed yet — the SHA-3 and SLH-DSA rounds are pure Rye plus Zig std.crypto/NIST KATs; will flag if SLH-DSA parity wants vendored FIPS 205 KAT vectors or a toolchain bump.
